Consider the following relational schema along with all the functional dependencies
that hold on them.
R1(A, B, C, D, E): { 𝐷→𝐸, 𝐸𝐴→𝐵, 𝐸𝐵→𝐶}
R2(A, B, C, D): { 𝐴→𝐷, 𝐴→𝐵, 𝐶→𝐴}
Which of the following statement(s) is/are TRUE?

options_latex.A:
SELECT S.name
FROM Students S
WHERE EXISTS (SELECT * FROM Enrolled E WHERE E.courseno = 1470 AND E.rollno = S.rollno);

options_latex.B:
SELECT S.name
FROM Students S
WHERE SIZEOF (SELECT * FROM Enrolled E WHERE E.courseno = 1470 AND E.rollno = S.rollno) > 0;

options_latex.C:
SELECT S.name
FROM Students S
WHERE 0 < (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Enrolled E WHERE E.courseno = 1470 AND E.rollno = S.rollno);

options_latex.D:
SELECT S.name
FROM Students S NATURAL JOIN Enrolled E
WHERE E.courseno = 1470;

